The Kaathe are a race of beings whose true bodies reside in a dream adjacent to Althane. In the world they are met through the orbs they use for locomotion: floating glass spheres, each lit from within with a single color. Hali's light is red, Tenno's blue, SeRaan's orange, and [[People/Althane/YuDaan|YuDaan's]] purple. Some orbs can pass unseen and some cannot; Hali's cannot.

An orb holds a Kaathe's memory. A Kaathe kept out of its orb for long loses itself: memory goes least important to most, and what fades returns only if the Kaathe is put back into the orb that stored it, if it has not decayed past recognition. A Kaathe given to a new orb keeps what it makes there, but nothing from the old.

The Kaathe can speak with one another over any distance, and a Kaathe in its orb can send word to any other it chooses.

[[Org/Althane/The Weft|The Weft]] have met [[People/Althane/Halidex Op-B|Hali]] and [[People/Althane/Tennobrin Er-K|Tenno]], and carry other orbs of the kind in their travels.
 The Kaathe homeworld is Orbits-Upon-Light, a place beyond the reach of most travelers; it keeps backups of a Kaathe's memory, and it has withdrawn from the rest of the Astra since the fall of the fourth sun.
